BRIEF: Design a single-storey Mediterranean garden house with three bedrooms and two bathrooms on a completely flat 60 by 48 metre site. Compose connected rectangular volumes in an asymmetric L shape around a sheltered garden. Use warm ivory plaster, pale limestone accents, terracotta pitched roofs with a clear main-roof hierarchy, a shaded entrance and generous room-proportioned glazing. Include a modern open-plan kitchen and dining area, comfortable private bedroom circulation, a covered veranda facing the garden, a modest swimming pool, a terrace and restrained planting. Keep the house coherent and fully editable, with no detached buildings, terrain changes or basement.
ACCEPTED DIRECTION: {"name":"Asymmetric Mediterranean Garden House","outdoorLiving":"The covered veranda faces directly into the sheltered garden and connects seamlessly to the open-plan kitchen, dining and living area through room-proportioned glazing. A limestone-toned terrace expands beside the veranda for dining and lounging, while a modest swimming pool is set within the garden court with clear sightlines from the social rooms.","landscape":"The flat site is treated as a restrained Mediterranean garden: clipped low hedging, gravel-edged planting beds, small groups of drought-tolerant shrubs, aromatic herbs and a limited number of slender shade trees. Planting frames the sheltered court, softens pool edges and preserves open arrival space around the connected house volumes."}
SITE: 60 x 48 m, flat, no terrain.
SWIMMING POOL: required by the brief
ENTRANCE: main door faces s; court 5.0 x 4.0 m.
VERANDAS: garden-veranda faces s, 11.0 x 6.0 m
