          "text": "{\"name\":\"Asymmetric Mediterranean Garden House\",\"concept\":\"A single-storey Mediterranean garden house formed as a connected asymmetric L around a sheltered, inward-looking garden. The longer social wing combines open-plan kitchen, dining and living spaces with generous garden glazing and a covered veranda; the shorter private wing provides three bedrooms and two bathrooms along calm, comfortable circulation. Warm ivory plaster, pale limestone detailing and terracotta pitched roofs establish a clear main-roof hierarchy without detached structures or changes in terrain.\",\"hierarchy\":[\"A dominant pitched-roof social wing anchors the composition and contains the open-plan kitchen, dining and living rooms facing the sheltered garden.\",\"A lower, perpendicular private wing forms the second arm of the L, containing three bedrooms, two bathrooms and a quiet internal circulation spine.\",\"A recessed shaded entrance sits at the inside bend of the L, mediating between arrival and the protected garden court.\",\"A covered veranda extends from the social wing toward the garden, with the terrace and modest pool positioned as integrated outdoor rooms rather than separate objects.\"],\"roofLanguage\":\"Terracotta clay-tile pitched roofs give the house its Mediterranean character. A broad, dominant main roof covers the social wing, while a lower perpendicular pitched roof distinguishes the bedroom wing. Deep eaves shade glazing and veranda edges; roof junctions remain simple and legible, reinforcing the asymmetric L-shaped massing.\",\"entrance\":\"A shaded, recessed entrance is placed at the protected inner corner of the L. Pale limestone threshold, surround and restrained wall detailing give arrival a durable civic emphasis, while the approach remains deliberately modest and sheltered beneath the roof overhang.\",\"outdoorLiving\":\"The covered veranda faces directly into the sheltered garden and connects seamlessly to the open-plan kitchen, dining and living area through room-proportioned glazing. A limestone-toned terrace expands beside the veranda for dining and lounging, while a modest swimming pool is set within the garden court with clear sightlines from the social rooms.\",\"landscape\":\"The flat site is treated as a restrained Mediterranean garden: clipped low hedging, gravel-edged planting beds, small groups of drought-tolerant shrubs, aromatic herbs and a limited number of slender shade trees. Planting frames the sheltered court, softens pool edges and preserves open arrival space around the connected house volumes.\",\"palette\":{\"walls\":\"ivory\",\"accent\":\"limestone\",\"roof\":\"bronze\",\"roofColor\":\"#B65A36\",\"deck\":\"limestone\"}}"
